1
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:53,471
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

2
00:00:53,596 --> 00:00:54,430
ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:54,555 --> 00:00:55,389
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

4
00:00:55,514 --> 00:00:56,348
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

5
00:01:15,868 --> 00:01:16,952
How about some breakfast?

6
00:01:18,037 --> 00:01:19,622
Since fate brought us together.

7
00:01:20,414 --> 00:01:22,708
I brought something for a hangover.

8
00:01:48,651 --> 00:01:51,695
<i>Bambi is so cute. Has she been adopted?</i>

9
00:01:58,577 --> 00:01:59,870
How does it taste?

10
00:02:03,082 --> 00:02:03,916
Good.

11
00:02:07,294 --> 00:02:09,922
- About last night--
- He's a real pain when drunk, isn't he?

12
00:02:11,549 --> 00:02:14,301
He clings to you and passes out.

13
00:02:15,678 --> 00:02:17,763
Then nothing wakes him up, right?

14
00:02:17,888 --> 00:02:19,056
Hey.

15
00:02:19,181 --> 00:02:20,432
Why do you like him?

16
00:02:28,399 --> 00:02:30,150
Su-a, get up. I'll take you home.

17
00:02:31,569 --> 00:02:32,987
Because he's wonderful.

18
00:02:35,948 --> 00:02:37,408
I think...

19
00:02:40,452 --> 00:02:42,913
he's the greatest person I know.

20
00:03:29,877 --> 00:03:30,836
Are you mad?

21
00:03:31,503 --> 00:03:33,130
You should be mad.

22
00:03:33,923 --> 00:03:36,467
My ex just barged into my apartment.

23
00:03:37,009 --> 00:03:39,511
You should've kicked my shins,
not join us for breakfast.

24
00:03:40,554 --> 00:03:42,473
I didn't want to make trouble for you.

25
00:03:43,349 --> 00:03:45,392
She would've gotten the wrong idea.

26
00:03:46,602 --> 00:03:47,895
Come on.

27
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:49,605
We were fully dressed.

28
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:53,984
Besides, when I'm drunk,
I just sleep like a baby for six hours.

29
00:03:54,109 --> 00:03:55,986
Lee Mi-do knows that better than anyone.

30
00:03:56,737 --> 00:03:57,863
Not true.

31
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:01,659
Something happened between us.

32
00:04:10,501 --> 00:04:11,794
Your acting's gotten good.

33
00:04:11,919 --> 00:04:13,462
I almost believed you.

34
00:04:14,672 --> 00:04:16,256
Thanks for seeing me home.

35
00:04:19,843 --> 00:04:22,388
Hey, don't joke about stuff like that.

36
00:04:23,847 --> 00:04:25,432
Come to think of it.

37
00:04:25,975 --> 00:04:28,727
Your door lock passcode
being your ex's birthday

38
00:04:28,852 --> 00:04:30,187
does annoy me.

39
00:04:58,465 --> 00:05:00,801
We're here, okay?

40
00:05:02,094 --> 00:05:02,928
LEE MI-DO

41
00:05:03,053 --> 00:05:05,055
- Take your shoes off.
- I don't want to.

42
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:07,558
Hold on, wait a second. Almost there.

43
00:05:07,683 --> 00:05:09,351
Lie down here.

44
00:05:09,476 --> 00:05:10,769
Here you go.

45
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:42,051
Mr. Namgung.

46
00:05:43,677 --> 00:05:45,763
I lied to you again.

47
00:05:47,765 --> 00:05:49,600
I want to make you happy...

48
00:05:51,185 --> 00:05:53,062
every single second

49
00:05:54,563 --> 00:05:56,148
we spend together,

50
00:05:58,192 --> 00:06:00,819
not just for a second.

51
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:05,574
That's my goal.

52
00:06:09,036 --> 00:06:11,163
I'll only stay for ten minutes.

53
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,792
Ten minutes is okay, right?

54
00:06:40,025 --> 00:06:41,235
We need to talk.

55
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:43,195
We're broken up right now.

56
00:06:43,987 --> 00:06:44,988
Don't apologize.

57
00:06:45,114 --> 00:06:46,657
Who said I was apologizing?

58
00:06:49,743 --> 00:06:51,411
Change your door lock code.

59
00:06:51,954 --> 00:06:53,080
I'll change mine too.

60
00:06:54,206 --> 00:06:55,457
And for the remaining time,

61
00:06:55,582 --> 00:06:57,751
let's not visit each other's places.

62
00:07:03,882 --> 00:07:04,883
I'll change it.

63
00:07:05,634 --> 00:07:07,469
If you're done, please leave.

64
00:07:07,594 --> 00:07:10,013
I don't want us
visiting each other's places

65
00:07:10,139 --> 00:07:11,765
starting right now.

66
00:07:12,683 --> 00:07:15,144
I felt bad until I took Park Su-a home.

67
00:07:17,062 --> 00:07:20,858
But on the way home, a thought hit me.

68
00:07:23,902 --> 00:07:25,445
"Is this what she wanted?"

69
00:07:28,949 --> 00:07:30,659
You said you wanted to get hurt.

70
00:07:31,910 --> 00:07:33,162
How does it feel?

71
00:07:35,289 --> 00:07:36,248
Like shit.

72
00:07:38,167 --> 00:07:39,251
Disgusting.

73
00:07:41,879 --> 00:07:42,838
What about you?

74
00:07:43,755 --> 00:07:44,798
Do you feel good?

75
00:07:45,883 --> 00:07:46,717
No.

76
00:07:48,552 --> 00:07:49,845
It feels like shit.

77
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:53,724
And disgusting.

78
00:08:05,611 --> 00:08:11,491
11. HOW DO WE LOVE, HOW DO WE LIVE?

79
00:08:20,292 --> 00:08:23,420
<i>Bambi is so cute. Has she been adopted?</i>

80
00:08:29,426 --> 00:08:31,720
BAMBI

81
00:08:31,845 --> 00:08:35,098
LOVABLE BAMBI IS LOOKING FOR A NEW FAMILY

82
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:00,749
Come on, smile.

83
00:09:02,459 --> 00:09:04,127
We'll break up in about ten days.

84
00:09:04,253 --> 00:09:05,087
You're mean.

85
00:09:20,477 --> 00:09:21,311
All right.

86
00:09:22,229 --> 00:09:24,273
I get that you can't leave Namgung Ho.

87
00:09:24,398 --> 00:09:25,941
I'll accept that.

88
00:09:28,026 --> 00:09:30,696
You still have to keep seeing me
for the remaining time.

89
00:09:30,821 --> 00:09:32,072
No takebacks on that.

90
00:09:32,823 --> 00:09:34,616
You can at least do that.

91
00:09:34,741 --> 00:09:37,035
It's not like it's that hard.

92
00:09:38,453 --> 00:09:40,706
Tell me if you've pulled
any secret stunts.

93
00:09:42,416 --> 00:09:43,959
Including digging into my past.

94
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:47,379
I haven't.

95
00:09:50,465 --> 00:09:51,758
I really haven't.

96
00:09:51,883 --> 00:09:54,136
Apart from looking into both your pasts.

97
00:09:55,095 --> 00:09:55,929
Nothing else.

98
00:10:03,979 --> 00:10:04,896
And your meds?

99
00:10:06,356 --> 00:10:07,399
Are you taking them?

100
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:10,152
When did it start?

101
00:10:12,738 --> 00:10:17,117
Meds won't cure my sociopathic tendencies.

102
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,077
They won't help.

103
00:10:19,202 --> 00:10:20,912
You know that's not what I mean.

104
00:10:27,294 --> 00:10:29,463
Can't you just pretend not to notice?

105
00:10:40,182 --> 00:10:41,308
If I tell you,

106
00:10:44,353 --> 00:10:45,562
will you sleep with me?

107
00:11:09,252 --> 00:11:10,087
Ms. Lee.

108
00:11:11,213 --> 00:11:12,422
Just so you know,

109
00:11:12,547 --> 00:11:14,049
I'm not a minor.

110
00:11:17,803 --> 00:11:19,888
And obviously, you're not either.

111
00:11:20,889 --> 00:11:23,892
Two voting-age adults
shouldn't be this innocent.

112
00:11:24,726 --> 00:11:26,895
This is hurting the birth rate.

113
00:11:34,194 --> 00:11:35,487
That was just...

114
00:11:36,279 --> 00:11:37,197
a joke.

115
00:11:41,743 --> 00:11:43,787
Just stay with me until I fall asleep.

116
00:11:48,333 --> 00:11:49,251
Have a seat.

117
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:07,269
I think it's because of you.

118
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:11,606
It started out of nowhere four months ago.

119
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:15,735
There's really no other reason...

120
00:12:16,319 --> 00:12:18,488
Then you should've come to Ahyeon-dong.

121
00:12:19,531 --> 00:12:21,741
They found you in Myeong-dong, right?

122
00:12:23,076 --> 00:12:24,953
I heard what the police said.

123
00:12:34,087 --> 00:12:36,590
In the time we have left,

124
00:12:38,175 --> 00:12:39,593
I'll find out for you.

125
00:12:41,303 --> 00:12:43,180
I'll find out the reason

126
00:12:44,139 --> 00:12:45,682
you keep going to Myeong-dong.

127
00:12:47,726 --> 00:12:48,602
Why?

128
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:52,647
Because you feel sorry for me?

129
00:12:53,273 --> 00:12:54,858
Because you'll dump me soon?

130
00:12:55,734 --> 00:12:57,068
To ease your guilt?

131
00:13:02,616 --> 00:13:03,658
No.

132
00:13:05,702 --> 00:13:07,078
I hate seeing you suffer.

133
00:13:09,247 --> 00:13:12,459
I just want you to stop hurting.

134
00:13:28,016 --> 00:13:30,227
GEUMSEOK TEAHOUSE

135
00:13:40,278 --> 00:13:42,405
- When did you start?
- Last September.

136
00:13:42,531 --> 00:13:44,115
So you joined my team because...

137
00:13:44,241 --> 00:13:46,576
I needed the sample dates.

138
00:13:48,078 --> 00:13:49,287
Is that really all?

139
00:13:51,498 --> 00:13:53,041
Of course.

140
00:13:53,667 --> 00:13:55,502
Why else would I join this team?

141
00:13:57,379 --> 00:13:59,130
It could be because of someone.

142
00:13:59,923 --> 00:14:02,133
Someone you've always dreamed
of working with

143
00:14:02,259 --> 00:14:04,386
and watched with a racing heart.

144
00:14:12,143 --> 00:14:13,937
You joined to work with me.

145
00:14:17,190 --> 00:14:18,608
I knew it.

146
00:14:18,733 --> 00:14:21,319
A Hunmin Confectionery legend,
the top recruit,

147
00:14:21,444 --> 00:14:23,530
and the youngest lead
behind Hot Chocolate Chips.

148
00:14:23,655 --> 00:14:26,366
So you came to work with me.

149
00:14:28,201 --> 00:14:29,035
I get it.

150
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:33,665
Now that I've shown you my hand,

151
00:14:33,790 --> 00:14:34,958
please share what you found.

152
00:14:35,083 --> 00:14:37,043
You want to cut a deal with just that?

153
00:14:37,168 --> 00:14:38,503
Based on your time off,

154
00:14:38,628 --> 00:14:40,714
you only started investigating
two months ago.

155
00:14:40,839 --> 00:14:44,342
You'd think you filmed
the sweet potato swap or something.

156
00:14:47,596 --> 00:14:49,139
How did you know?

157
00:14:53,059 --> 00:14:54,227
I'd feel inadequate, too.

158
00:14:55,770 --> 00:14:58,398
You started last year, while I only needed

159
00:14:59,149 --> 00:15:00,650
two months to film the video.

160
00:15:00,775 --> 00:15:03,737
Now you see why I'm the legend
of Hunmin Confectionery?

161
00:15:06,072 --> 00:15:07,282
Did you really film it?

162
00:15:09,284 --> 00:15:11,244
I'll let you in on my plan.

163
00:15:11,369 --> 00:15:13,204
On one condition.

164
00:15:14,956 --> 00:15:17,917
Never trust that bastard Namgung Ho.

165
00:15:32,515 --> 00:15:33,350
Deok-sun.

166
00:15:34,601 --> 00:15:36,186
Your fantasy is all wrong.

167
00:15:36,311 --> 00:15:38,104
A good man doesn't cook for you.

168
00:15:38,229 --> 00:15:40,357
He treats you to fine dining.

169
00:15:41,858 --> 00:15:43,777
<i>I thought you might misunderstand,</i>

170
00:15:43,902 --> 00:15:45,403
<i>so I'm telling you this now.</i>

171
00:15:45,528 --> 00:15:48,323
That bastard Namgung Ho isn't on our side.

172
00:15:48,448 --> 00:15:50,450
He went over to Procurement long ago.

173
00:15:50,575 --> 00:15:52,827
That bastard Namgung Ho

174
00:15:52,952 --> 00:15:55,789
got me completely wasted
and stole my work phone.

175
00:15:56,831 --> 00:15:58,541
The footage is on it.

176
00:15:58,667 --> 00:16:01,628
We have to find that phone.

177
00:16:01,753 --> 00:16:04,255
It's definitely at Namgung Ho's place.

178
00:16:09,678 --> 00:16:10,970
I want some banana milk.

179
00:16:13,014 --> 00:16:16,017
I love having banana milk with my steak.

180
00:17:39,559 --> 00:17:41,269
Some grease splattered on the floor.

181
00:17:41,394 --> 00:17:42,937
And I love cleaning.

182
00:17:49,527 --> 00:17:50,737
Wipe it clean.

183
00:17:51,654 --> 00:17:52,864
Okay.

184
00:17:58,077 --> 00:17:59,913
Did Ho-sik say to find his phone?

185
00:18:01,998 --> 00:18:03,750
Is that guy delusional?

186
00:18:04,417 --> 00:18:07,504
He got drunk and lost it,
so why treat me like a thief?

187
00:18:08,254 --> 00:18:10,965
That area is full of thieves
who steal phones.

188
00:18:12,550 --> 00:18:15,136
It's probably in Thailand
or Vietnam by now.

189
00:18:16,429 --> 00:18:17,388
Right?

190
00:18:17,972 --> 00:18:19,390
He was mistaken, right?

191
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:24,062
I knew it!

192
00:18:24,729 --> 00:18:28,316
I only looked just in case.
I never believed him.

193
00:18:28,441 --> 00:18:30,068
You and Procurement? No way.

194
00:18:31,361 --> 00:18:32,529
I did get an offer.

195
00:18:35,031 --> 00:18:37,575
I saw Jeong Yeon-ho rig the sugar test.

196
00:18:41,037 --> 00:18:42,413
I tried to ignore it,

197
00:18:43,206 --> 00:18:45,166
but they won't let it go.

198
00:18:48,586 --> 00:18:52,924
<i>Marlon Brando has this line
in</i> The Godfather.

199
00:18:54,509 --> 00:18:56,386
"Keep your friends close,

200
00:18:57,011 --> 00:18:59,389
but your enemies closer."

201
00:19:01,224 --> 00:19:02,767
In the spirit of that,

202
00:19:02,892 --> 00:19:05,061
after much thought, I have decided

203
00:19:05,186 --> 00:19:07,230
to take you under my wing.

204
00:19:07,355 --> 00:19:09,023
You really don't have to.

205
00:19:09,732 --> 00:19:10,567
Pardon?

206
00:19:13,152 --> 00:19:14,654
I'll pretend I didn't see anything.

207
00:19:18,241 --> 00:19:19,075
I mean it.

208
00:19:21,578 --> 00:19:22,412
I swear.

209
00:19:24,038 --> 00:19:26,165
Does this sound like a joke to you?

210
00:19:27,584 --> 00:19:29,627
Does it sound like I'm joking to you?

211
00:19:29,752 --> 00:19:33,548
Look, I'm being serious here.

212
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:36,968
I'm offering you an opportunity.
Don't you see?

213
00:19:37,093 --> 00:19:38,136
Opportunity, my foot.

214
00:19:38,803 --> 00:19:40,763
You messed up and I caught you,

215
00:19:40,889 --> 00:19:43,182
so you're trying to cover it up.

216
00:19:45,727 --> 00:19:50,064
Sure. I admit anyone would want
a talent like mine on their team.

217
00:19:50,189 --> 00:19:52,150
You've got the wrong idea.

218
00:19:52,275 --> 00:19:54,485
This isn't damage control. I was--

219
00:19:54,611 --> 00:19:56,988
It wasn't Marlon Brando. It was Al Pacino.

220
00:19:59,324 --> 00:20:00,158
Pardon?

221
00:20:00,283 --> 00:20:01,868
"Keep your friends close,

222
00:20:03,828 --> 00:20:05,496
but your enemies closer."

223
00:20:05,622 --> 00:20:07,665
Al Pacino said that.

224
00:20:07,790 --> 00:20:10,168
That's from <i>The Godfather Part II.</i>

225
00:20:10,293 --> 00:20:12,003
Marlon Brando dies in the first one.

226
00:20:14,255 --> 00:20:15,882
You haven't seen it, have you?

227
00:20:16,007 --> 00:20:17,759
Sorry. I spoiled it.

228
00:20:19,636 --> 00:20:21,512
That's not the point right now.

229
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:24,015
You turned them down, right?

230
00:20:24,724 --> 00:20:25,683
No.

231
00:20:26,559 --> 00:20:27,810
I'm thinking about it.

232
00:20:27,936 --> 00:20:29,646
Honestly, I was tempted.

233
00:20:30,438 --> 00:20:34,025
For a guy with no connections,
those chances don't come often.

234
00:20:34,150 --> 00:20:37,195
I only hung out with them
to test the waters.

235
00:20:44,786 --> 00:20:46,746
I don't think I can eat with you.

236
00:20:47,330 --> 00:20:48,706
I'll be going now.

237
00:21:23,032 --> 00:21:24,242
What are you doing?

238
00:21:24,367 --> 00:21:25,576
Nothing worked.

239
00:21:27,704 --> 00:21:30,915
I tried your birthday,
your phone number,

240
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:33,918
the release date of <i>The 13th Season,</i>
and your hire date.

241
00:21:34,043 --> 00:21:36,504
How do you know my hire date when I don't?

242
00:21:37,213 --> 00:21:38,381
You're unbelievable.

243
00:21:38,506 --> 00:21:41,259
Do I really know nothing about you?

244
00:21:48,141 --> 00:21:48,975
I'm hungry.

245
00:21:49,100 --> 00:21:51,185
I should eat before I go.

246
00:22:03,740 --> 00:22:05,366
What was my hire date?

247
00:22:05,491 --> 00:22:07,160
March 12, 2018.

248
00:22:09,037 --> 00:22:11,039
Do you know my first department?

249
00:22:11,164 --> 00:22:13,249
- Sales.
- Are you stalking me?

250
00:22:15,752 --> 00:22:17,879
I heard it from Sang-hun.

251
00:22:18,421 --> 00:22:21,591
I checked with Sales about the survey,
and he said you were from Sales.

252
00:22:22,425 --> 00:22:23,718
That's how I know.

253
00:22:27,847 --> 00:22:29,057
It's true.

254
00:22:36,564 --> 00:22:37,565
Then do you also know...

255
00:22:39,358 --> 00:22:41,903
that I spent a year in Sales
being an outcast?

256
00:22:44,405 --> 00:22:46,324
I was their star rookie.

257
00:22:47,950 --> 00:22:52,080
The top sales team groomed me
as their star recruit.

258
00:22:55,083 --> 00:22:59,170
Two months in, I landed a retail deal
and doubled our sales.

259
00:23:01,172 --> 00:23:02,757
Back then, I thought...

260
00:23:04,592 --> 00:23:06,844
I'd make director at least.

261
00:23:09,639 --> 00:23:11,516
About six months into the job?

262
00:23:13,184 --> 00:23:15,394
We had team drinks with a buyer,

263
00:23:16,270 --> 00:23:19,315
and he gave little cash envelopes
to our team members.

264
00:23:21,943 --> 00:23:23,820
But I said I was okay and declined.

265
00:23:24,654 --> 00:23:26,197
And starting the next day,

266
00:23:27,031 --> 00:23:29,784
things started happening
that weren't okay at all.

267
00:23:47,426 --> 00:23:48,636
Let me see your finger.

268
00:24:12,451 --> 00:24:15,413
It was 300,000 won. Just 300,000 won.

269
00:24:16,664 --> 00:24:18,499
In that envelope.

270
00:24:20,793 --> 00:24:21,961
I was so bitter.

271
00:24:23,504 --> 00:24:25,798
My conscience was only worth 300,000 won.

272
00:24:31,220 --> 00:24:35,308
So this time,
I'm going to sell it for a lot more.

273
00:24:37,268 --> 00:24:38,269
Well?

274
00:24:38,853 --> 00:24:40,479
Do you still think I'm wonderful?

275
00:24:44,275 --> 00:24:47,278
Park Su-a, you don't know me
as well as you think.

276
00:24:48,696 --> 00:24:50,615
I'm not the person you think I am.

277
00:24:51,282 --> 00:24:52,825
Make sure you remember that.

278
00:24:52,950 --> 00:24:53,868
And that...

279
00:24:56,579 --> 00:24:58,331
fantasies don't exist in this world.

280
00:25:08,591 --> 00:25:10,384
RAW MATERIAL MARGIN CALCULATION

281
00:25:10,509 --> 00:25:12,929
HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY
SWEET POTATO SCANDAL RELATIONSHIP MAP

282
00:25:13,095 --> 00:25:14,972
EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR YOON

283
00:25:23,231 --> 00:25:25,024
<i>I'm not the person you think I am.</i>

284
00:25:25,983 --> 00:25:27,526
Make sure you remember that.

285
00:25:27,652 --> 00:25:28,486
And...

286
00:25:30,529 --> 00:25:32,615
There's no fantasy in this world.

287
00:25:39,330 --> 00:25:40,748
Su-a, have some fruit...

288
00:25:43,084 --> 00:25:44,460
Did she go take a shower?

289
00:26:02,937 --> 00:26:05,189
<i>Rookie director Tak Se-yeong's film,</i>

290
00:26:05,314 --> 00:26:09,694
When I Woke Up in the Morning,
I Was a Dirt-Poor Job Seeker in Korea,

291
00:26:09,819 --> 00:26:11,529
<i>also known as "Dirt-Poor Job Seeker,"</i>

292
00:26:11,654 --> 00:26:13,781
<i>passed two million tickets
in just two months,</i>

293
00:26:13,906 --> 00:26:16,450
<i>becoming the year's biggest hit.</i>

294
00:26:16,575 --> 00:26:18,786
I checked the places
you said you've gone to

295
00:26:18,911 --> 00:26:20,079
in the past four months.

296
00:26:20,204 --> 00:26:22,498
<i>- A sleeper hit...</i>
- You weren't wandering.

297
00:26:22,623 --> 00:26:24,542
You were heading somewhere.

298
00:26:24,667 --> 00:26:27,461
<i>...the lead, a crown prince
in a fictional kingdom,</i>

299
00:26:27,586 --> 00:26:28,963
<i>crosses over to Korea...</i>

300
00:26:29,088 --> 00:26:32,383
Do you have any special memories
of Myeong-dong?

301
00:26:32,508 --> 00:26:35,177
<i>With its fresh premise
and unique world-building,</i>

302
00:26:35,303 --> 00:26:36,137
<i>it earned praise...</i>

303
00:26:36,262 --> 00:26:37,179
Are you listening?

304
00:26:38,764 --> 00:26:40,099
<i>Director Tak Se-yeong...</i>

305
00:26:40,224 --> 00:26:41,058
I remember.

306
00:26:41,183 --> 00:26:44,478
<i>...recognized for tight plotting
and genre instincts,</i>

307
00:26:44,603 --> 00:26:47,315
<i>has become Chungmuro's
most-watched rookie director--</i>

308
00:26:50,067 --> 00:26:51,694
You know,

309
00:26:51,819 --> 00:26:57,199
when the news talks
about someone else winning a lawsuit,

310
00:26:57,325 --> 00:26:59,493
it just really annoys me, too.

311
00:26:59,618 --> 00:27:01,329
Ugh, so annoying!

312
00:27:10,212 --> 00:27:11,172
Still not smiling?

313
00:27:16,302 --> 00:27:18,095
What will make you smile?

314
00:27:22,391 --> 00:27:24,060
I love seeing you smile.

315
00:27:31,108 --> 00:27:33,444
WOLMIDO AMUSEMENT PARK

316
00:27:37,615 --> 00:27:38,783
Stop!

317
00:27:42,495 --> 00:27:44,872
Wait!

318
00:27:46,415 --> 00:27:47,958
You can get on now.

319
00:27:50,795 --> 00:27:51,629
You coming?

320
00:28:18,948 --> 00:28:21,992
I can't ride it anymore.

321
00:28:27,039 --> 00:28:28,749
No way.

322
00:28:29,834 --> 00:28:30,793
No.

323
00:28:31,502 --> 00:28:33,712
No, I hate it. I can't.

324
00:28:34,547 --> 00:28:36,048
I mean, I won't.

325
00:28:36,173 --> 00:28:39,677
You said you wanted to see me smile
and would do anything.

326
00:28:40,344 --> 00:28:42,304
For the record,

327
00:28:42,888 --> 00:28:46,809
I never said I'd do anything.

328
00:28:48,853 --> 00:28:51,480
I asked what would make you smile.

329
00:28:55,693 --> 00:28:56,610
Why don't we...

330
00:28:57,194 --> 00:28:58,028
Oh.

331
00:28:58,571 --> 00:28:59,447
Go get food?

332
00:29:00,614 --> 00:29:02,324
Sashimi? How about sashimi?

333
00:29:02,450 --> 00:29:03,784
Rockfish.

334
00:29:03,909 --> 00:29:05,494
Rockfish is great. You in?

335
00:29:06,454 --> 00:29:09,206
I'll ride it alone.
You go eat your rockfish.

336
00:29:10,040 --> 00:29:12,460
Wait, hold on. Wait a second!

337
00:29:14,712 --> 00:29:18,507
Isn't 12 times enough already?

338
00:29:19,091 --> 00:29:20,342
How many more rides--

339
00:29:20,468 --> 00:29:21,844
I can't shake the fear.

340
00:29:24,430 --> 00:29:27,558
After ten times, I usually feel fine.

341
00:29:27,683 --> 00:29:30,603
But no matter how much I ride,
the fear won't go away.

342
00:29:38,277 --> 00:29:39,111
First...

343
00:29:41,989 --> 00:29:43,616
Let's get some nausea medicine.

344
00:30:07,389 --> 00:30:08,682
Put your hands up!

345
00:30:08,807 --> 00:30:09,767
Put my hands up?

346
00:30:18,943 --> 00:30:19,777
HAEON HALL

347
00:30:19,902 --> 00:30:23,781
Hey, did you see that movie?
What was it? <i>When I Woke Up Today?</i>

348
00:30:23,906 --> 00:30:26,325
No, wait. <i>Maybe When I Woke Up?</i>

349
00:30:27,409 --> 00:30:29,036
What was that title again?

350
00:30:29,703 --> 00:30:31,080
Oh, "Dirt-Poor Job Seeker."

351
00:30:31,205 --> 00:30:34,083
Oh, right.
Is the director really a rookie?

352
00:30:34,208 --> 00:30:36,919
Its mise-en-scène is better
than Park Chan-wook's.

353
00:30:37,044 --> 00:30:38,712
Tak Jackson made it big.

354
00:30:42,132 --> 00:30:43,676
Oh, he was a college classmate.

355
00:30:46,554 --> 00:30:50,182
That nerd finally made it big.
That's just like him.

356
00:30:51,225 --> 00:30:52,226
What should I do?

357
00:30:53,435 --> 00:30:54,687
I should just...

358
00:30:54,812 --> 00:30:57,606
- Want me to tell them to shut up?
- Don't you dare.

359
00:30:57,731 --> 00:30:58,857
I'll kill you.

360
00:31:09,410 --> 00:31:11,912
I told you this once.

361
00:31:13,581 --> 00:31:16,208
That you should get back up
if you feel embarrassed.

362
00:31:19,253 --> 00:31:21,505
But the truth is, I only stood up.

363
00:31:22,506 --> 00:31:24,300
I haven't taken a single step.

364
00:31:27,136 --> 00:31:30,014
It's an unfamiliar path,
and I'm terrified.

365
00:31:33,809 --> 00:31:36,228
Most of all, I'm exhausted.

366
00:31:37,479 --> 00:31:39,690
Passion, energy...

367
00:31:40,316 --> 00:31:41,859
Those are long gone.

368
00:31:41,984 --> 00:31:45,321
I don't even have courage,
let alone confidence.

369
00:31:52,077 --> 00:31:54,371
Everyone around me is doing so well.

370
00:31:58,167 --> 00:32:02,588
It terrifies me that deep down
I want them to fail.

371
00:32:04,923 --> 00:32:08,552
And that I'm too petty
to celebrate their success.

372
00:32:10,804 --> 00:32:14,391
I'm scared because I'm still not sure
if this is the right path for me.

373
00:32:15,351 --> 00:32:19,188
But turning back is even scarier.

374
00:32:32,868 --> 00:32:35,162
If you think I'm pathetic, so be it.

375
00:32:36,705 --> 00:32:37,706
This is

376
00:32:38,540 --> 00:32:40,209
just who I am right now.

377
00:32:52,012 --> 00:32:53,097
Oh, no.

378
00:32:56,642 --> 00:32:58,644
I think I really like you.

379
00:33:04,900 --> 00:33:05,943
Get up.

380
00:33:07,277 --> 00:33:10,531
I think I know exactly what to do for you.

381
00:33:14,284 --> 00:33:15,244
I'll do it.

382
00:33:16,662 --> 00:33:17,496
Let's go.

383
00:33:21,875 --> 00:33:23,168
This is supposed to help me?

384
00:33:23,293 --> 00:33:24,753
WHEN I WOKE UP IN THE MORNING,
I WAS A DIRT-POOR JOB SEEKER IN KOREA

385
00:33:24,878 --> 00:33:25,713
Yeah.

386
00:33:26,422 --> 00:33:28,298
You'd be scared to watch it alone.

387
00:33:29,341 --> 00:33:31,009
So I'm watching it with you.

388
00:33:34,722 --> 00:33:36,849
We can leave if you want.

389
00:33:36,974 --> 00:33:38,809
Even five minutes is fine.

390
00:33:40,436 --> 00:33:42,604
You'll dump me
when our month is over anyway.

391
00:33:44,440 --> 00:33:46,483
So who cares if you feel humiliated?

392
00:33:46,608 --> 00:33:48,485
Why worry about pride?

393
00:33:48,610 --> 00:33:50,404
We won't see each other again, right?

394
00:33:50,529 --> 00:33:51,739
Don't say that.

395
00:33:52,448 --> 00:33:55,200
If it makes you upset,
let me hold your hand.

396
00:33:58,746 --> 00:34:00,914
You'll be less scared, and I...

397
00:34:03,041 --> 00:34:04,001
I'll just like it.

398
00:34:19,266 --> 00:34:20,809
<i>I told you not to follow me.</i>

399
00:34:22,269 --> 00:34:23,937
<i>I take back what I said.</i>

400
00:34:28,192 --> 00:34:30,527
<i>What is pathetic is not this planet...</i>

401
00:34:33,071 --> 00:34:35,741
<i>but me, for running my mouth
without knowing how you feel.</i>

402
00:34:43,081 --> 00:34:44,458
Less scary with me, right?

403
00:35:02,100 --> 00:35:04,812
How long do I have to eat in silence?

404
00:35:13,695 --> 00:35:15,364
Just don't let Sang-su catch you.

405
00:35:16,782 --> 00:35:18,200
He's a teenager.

406
00:35:18,325 --> 00:35:19,868
Even if he's chill like me,

407
00:35:19,993 --> 00:35:22,329
your genes make him hold grudges.

408
00:35:24,665 --> 00:35:27,084
Frankly, it's not like you're remarrying.

409
00:35:27,209 --> 00:35:29,795
Even if he finds out, he won't care.

410
00:35:50,691 --> 00:35:51,984
Don't flatter yourself.

411
00:35:52,985 --> 00:35:54,403
I'm very happy.

412
00:35:55,195 --> 00:35:57,322
I'm not crying because I'm hung up on you.

413
00:36:02,452 --> 00:36:03,996
Why are you such a mess?

414
00:36:05,080 --> 00:36:06,748
Couldn't you do better?

415
00:36:06,874 --> 00:36:08,125
Hey.

416
00:36:08,250 --> 00:36:11,712
I feel bad being the only happy one.

417
00:36:13,797 --> 00:36:15,007
I thought

418
00:36:16,174 --> 00:36:18,510
I just wanted to brag to you.

419
00:36:19,720 --> 00:36:20,971
Guess I was wrong.

420
00:36:23,098 --> 00:36:24,224
I guess...

421
00:36:26,518 --> 00:36:28,770
I wanted you to congratulate me.

422
00:36:50,417 --> 00:36:52,628
"Midori4882" was you?

423
00:36:54,338 --> 00:36:55,839
Air out the place.

424
00:36:55,964 --> 00:36:57,424
I'm allergic to cats.

425
00:37:02,971 --> 00:37:04,806
How did you find my post about Bambi?

426
00:37:04,932 --> 00:37:06,767
None of your business.

427
00:37:07,559 --> 00:37:10,437
I'm going to ask you three questions.

428
00:37:11,897 --> 00:37:13,690
Whatever they are, I won't answer them.

429
00:37:16,568 --> 00:37:19,363
Namgung Ho did drag in middle school.
I'll show you.

430
00:37:24,660 --> 00:37:28,497
First, why did Namgung Ho move
to Procurement?

431
00:37:28,622 --> 00:37:33,418
Second, who got disciplined
for Namgung's mudflat accident?

432
00:37:33,543 --> 00:37:37,297
Third, the night you stayed at his place,

433
00:37:37,839 --> 00:37:40,050
who drank with Namgung Ho?

434
00:37:41,635 --> 00:37:43,095
I can't tell you that.

435
00:37:44,596 --> 00:37:46,139
He's really cute in drag.

436
00:37:49,601 --> 00:37:50,852
I am curious, sure.

437
00:37:51,979 --> 00:37:53,730
But you have no right to know.

438
00:37:53,855 --> 00:37:57,067
You're only doing this
to ease your own guilt.

439
00:37:58,110 --> 00:37:59,820
Yes, you're right.

440
00:38:00,654 --> 00:38:01,947
What's wrong with that?

441
00:38:03,657 --> 00:38:05,784
You really have no shame.

442
00:38:05,909 --> 00:38:06,910
Then again,

443
00:38:07,619 --> 00:38:10,080
I knew you had no shame
when I saw you eat Coco Jelly.

444
00:38:11,164 --> 00:38:12,541
Why bring up Coco Jelly?

445
00:38:12,666 --> 00:38:13,959
Coco Jelly

446
00:38:14,793 --> 00:38:16,169
is a Happy Confectionery product.

447
00:38:17,254 --> 00:38:20,173
After his rice-cake chicken
was ruined by Happy Confectionery,

448
00:38:20,298 --> 00:38:21,925
he never eats their products.

449
00:38:25,470 --> 00:38:28,348
Coco Jelly are the only gummies I eat
since middle school.

450
00:38:28,473 --> 00:38:33,061
Blame Hunmin Confectionery for not making
better gummies than Coco Jelly!

451
00:38:33,186 --> 00:38:36,023
If it makes you that mad,
step up and make one yourself.

452
00:38:36,148 --> 00:38:39,109
The Candy Department handles gummies.
I'm in the Snack Department!

453
00:38:47,909 --> 00:38:50,412
I don't want to talk anymore.
Please leave.

454
00:39:05,761 --> 00:39:06,803
I came for you.

455
00:39:09,181 --> 00:39:11,475
- I was curious about you.
- Why?

456
00:39:12,392 --> 00:39:13,602
Why are you curious?

457
00:39:14,186 --> 00:39:15,228
I wonder, too.

458
00:39:16,271 --> 00:39:18,023
Why am I so curious about you?

459
00:39:21,902 --> 00:39:24,362
Pulling a crazy stunt like this,

460
00:39:24,488 --> 00:39:26,573
and coming all the way here.

461
00:39:31,620 --> 00:39:33,955
Why am I so freaking curious about you?

462
00:39:40,253 --> 00:39:43,757
Let's just say this is why I came today.

463
00:39:47,427 --> 00:39:48,887
Give it back. It's mine.

464
00:39:49,930 --> 00:39:51,765
No, it isn't. It's mine.

465
00:39:51,890 --> 00:39:53,892
Namgung Ho drew it, so it's his,

466
00:39:54,017 --> 00:39:56,520
and what's his is mine,
so this is mine too.

467
00:39:58,396 --> 00:40:00,107
No, it's mine.

468
00:40:00,232 --> 00:40:02,275
He drew it for me, so it's mine!

469
00:40:09,533 --> 00:40:11,159
- Give it back! Damn it!
- Let go!

470
00:40:11,284 --> 00:40:12,744
- I said it's mine!
- It's mine!

471
00:40:12,869 --> 00:40:13,912
- No!
- Damn it!

472
00:40:14,579 --> 00:40:15,872
Let go!

473
00:40:15,997 --> 00:40:16,998
- Hey!
- Hey!

474
00:40:18,333 --> 00:40:20,168
Damn it, seriously!

475
00:40:21,128 --> 00:40:22,462
- Hey!
- Hey!

476
00:40:23,130 --> 00:40:24,172
Give it to me!

477
00:40:25,298 --> 00:40:26,800
I said it's mine!

478
00:40:35,433 --> 00:40:37,561
Are you insane? What is this even...

479
00:40:42,190 --> 00:40:43,358
Can't you...

480
00:40:45,443 --> 00:40:47,362
just give it to me?

481
00:40:48,613 --> 00:40:50,323
I know I have no right.

482
00:40:51,950 --> 00:40:53,994
And I know I have no shame.

483
00:40:58,874 --> 00:41:01,001
But could you just give it to me?

484
00:41:05,714 --> 00:41:07,883
I've been looking for it forever.

485
00:41:09,759 --> 00:41:12,053
I wanted it so badly.

486
00:41:16,725 --> 00:41:17,767
Please.

487
00:41:19,394 --> 00:41:20,729
Can't I have it?

488
00:41:34,659 --> 00:41:36,953
<i>I'd been looking for it forever.</i>

489
00:41:37,787 --> 00:41:40,081
<i>I wanted it so badly.</i>

490
00:41:42,167 --> 00:41:43,001
Huge news, guys!

491
00:41:44,336 --> 00:41:47,464
- Manager Jeong lost it yesterday.
- That's not huge news.

492
00:41:47,589 --> 00:41:50,175
He causes trouble every other day.

493
00:41:50,300 --> 00:41:53,178
But this one's pretty big.

494
00:41:53,303 --> 00:41:56,139
He got drunk with a client
and clocked him in the jaw.

495
00:41:57,474 --> 00:41:58,516
Serves him right.

496
00:41:59,100 --> 00:42:00,644
I hope he gets sued.

497
00:42:00,769 --> 00:42:02,771
They're already threatening to sue.

498
00:42:02,896 --> 00:42:04,231
Mr. Namgung went to beg.

499
00:42:05,273 --> 00:42:06,316
- What?
- Pardon?

500
00:42:08,026 --> 00:42:09,569
Yeah, he's there right now.

501
00:42:19,621 --> 00:42:22,707
This was attempted murder. You hear me?

502
00:42:23,792 --> 00:42:24,793
DAEPYEONG MILLING

503
00:42:24,918 --> 00:42:25,919
Forget that.

504
00:42:26,044 --> 00:42:28,755
Rewrite the contract with a 15% bump.

505
00:42:30,507 --> 00:42:34,177
And don't even think
about getting on your knees.

506
00:42:34,302 --> 00:42:36,972
I don't have any sympathy for that.

507
00:42:37,097 --> 00:42:38,056
Got it?

508
00:42:40,183 --> 00:42:41,643
I have no intention to.

509
00:42:43,436 --> 00:42:45,230
I hate humiliating myself.

510
00:42:53,113 --> 00:42:54,364
You have a cool name.

511
00:42:54,489 --> 00:42:56,741
CEO CHOI YEONG-DO

512
00:43:02,622 --> 00:43:04,040
Stop! What are you doing?

513
00:43:04,165 --> 00:43:05,083
Don't! No, stop!

514
00:43:05,208 --> 00:43:06,584
Stop, don't!

515
00:43:06,710 --> 00:43:08,753
No!

516
00:43:13,174 --> 00:43:14,843
I guess CEO Choi was really mad.

517
00:43:14,968 --> 00:43:17,095
CEO CHOI YEONG-DO

518
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:21,850
- Are you okay?
- Thank you.

519
00:43:23,059 --> 00:43:24,686
You bastard! Are you crazy?

520
00:43:24,811 --> 00:43:25,854
Look at the blood!

521
00:43:26,980 --> 00:43:27,814
You crazy bastard.

522
00:43:28,606 --> 00:43:29,983
I'm fine.

523
00:43:30,108 --> 00:43:31,901
If this helps calm your anger,

524
00:43:32,027 --> 00:43:34,070
I'm ready to take more hits.

525
00:43:37,282 --> 00:43:38,199
No.

526
00:43:39,409 --> 00:43:40,618
That's not true.

527
00:43:41,494 --> 00:43:42,829
I didn't throw that!

528
00:43:42,954 --> 00:43:45,290
Let's call it even
for yesterday's assault.

529
00:43:46,499 --> 00:43:48,209
I'll see you at the next meeting.

530
00:44:15,779 --> 00:44:17,113
MANAGER EOM HO-SIK

531
00:44:17,238 --> 00:44:18,281
PROCUREMENT NEVER RESTS

532
00:44:18,406 --> 00:44:20,158
YOU DIDN'T MESS UP, RIGHT?

533
00:44:31,544 --> 00:44:34,672
Should a manager really be slacking off
in broad daylight?

534
00:44:35,840 --> 00:44:37,801
After a six-month pay cut

535
00:44:38,468 --> 00:44:40,136
and being passed over for promotion,

536
00:44:40,261 --> 00:44:42,013
I've earned some slacking off.

537
00:44:43,556 --> 00:44:44,682
Damn it.

538
00:44:45,850 --> 00:44:47,977
If only I hadn't lost that phone.

539
00:44:49,312 --> 00:44:51,022
I caught them red-handed.

540
00:44:52,190 --> 00:44:55,568
Hey, did you really not take that phone?

541
00:44:55,693 --> 00:44:58,113
The thieves who took your phone were pros.

542
00:44:59,572 --> 00:45:02,575
It was probably pawned
and shipped across the Pacific.

543
00:45:02,700 --> 00:45:05,161
No, it's definitely still in Korea.

544
00:45:06,204 --> 00:45:08,415
Even if I have to search every pawnshop,

545
00:45:08,540 --> 00:45:09,958
I'll definitely find it.

546
00:45:15,505 --> 00:45:17,215
Change your mind while you can.

547
00:45:18,675 --> 00:45:21,636
I don't know why you suddenly
want to play Superman.

548
00:45:22,429 --> 00:45:24,264
Just be Superman for Su-min.

549
00:45:26,015 --> 00:45:27,559
My daughter Su-min

550
00:45:28,309 --> 00:45:30,854
went to the International Luce
Piano Competition.

551
00:45:31,980 --> 00:45:33,314
It's quite a mouthful.

552
00:45:34,107 --> 00:45:36,025
She made it to the finals again.

553
00:45:37,152 --> 00:45:39,571
That's why I have to make director.

554
00:45:39,696 --> 00:45:41,865
Otherwise, I can't support her.

555
00:45:42,699 --> 00:45:44,117
So I will make director.

556
00:45:46,119 --> 00:45:47,662
I can't help you.

557
00:45:48,997 --> 00:45:51,791
I thought that material disposal audit

558
00:45:51,916 --> 00:45:53,835
made my position clear enough.

559
00:45:55,837 --> 00:45:58,339
I know you did that on purpose to stop me.

560
00:46:03,970 --> 00:46:04,888
That's not true.

561
00:46:05,013 --> 00:46:06,931
I did it to impress Procurement.

562
00:46:10,602 --> 00:46:13,938
Would being on their good side
make you happy?

563
00:46:15,023 --> 00:46:16,941
I didn't call you here to join me.

564
00:46:18,193 --> 00:46:21,654
I called you to stop you
from doing what you're doing.

565
00:46:26,826 --> 00:46:28,036
The next batter's up.

566
00:46:30,622 --> 00:46:31,956
I'll get going.

567
00:46:40,173 --> 00:46:42,091
PRIME ON CONVENIENCE STORE

568
00:46:44,135 --> 00:46:46,387
I touched it earlier, and it opened up.

569
00:46:53,770 --> 00:46:55,063
It's only two stitches.

570
00:46:57,524 --> 00:46:58,983
They said it won't scar.

571
00:46:59,108 --> 00:47:00,902
Transfer to another department.

572
00:47:02,904 --> 00:47:05,698
I can't get you back
on the TF team this year.

573
00:47:05,823 --> 00:47:07,825
Unless we find Manager Eom's phone.

574
00:47:09,744 --> 00:47:11,746
There are more files to investigate.

575
00:47:11,871 --> 00:47:13,039
So request a transfer.

576
00:47:13,164 --> 00:47:15,917
Forget it. It's too much trouble.

577
00:47:20,630 --> 00:47:21,756
It's for Ms. Lee, right?

578
00:47:22,840 --> 00:47:24,592
You live like this,

579
00:47:25,343 --> 00:47:27,387
enduring this misery,

580
00:47:28,763 --> 00:47:29,973
all for Ms. Lee, right?

581
00:47:35,520 --> 00:47:37,605
Why are you bringing her up?

582
00:47:38,439 --> 00:47:40,984
Because Lee Mi-do
puts a brake on your life.

583
00:47:42,235 --> 00:47:43,987
Stopping the investigation,

584
00:47:44,112 --> 00:47:46,864
enduring all this humiliation
working in Procurement,

585
00:47:46,990 --> 00:47:47,824
and even...

586
00:47:50,618 --> 00:47:52,495
dating me when your heart wasn't in it...

587
00:47:54,414 --> 00:47:56,416
It was all for Lee Mi-do, wasn't it?

588
00:48:00,420 --> 00:48:01,754
Does she even know?

589
00:48:03,548 --> 00:48:06,092
That you're dying inside because of her?

590
00:48:06,217 --> 00:48:09,053
That your life is completely colorless?
Does she have any idea?

591
00:48:09,178 --> 00:48:12,098
Park Su-a, stop it.
You're crossing the line.

592
00:48:12,223 --> 00:48:13,683
Then I'll cross it even further.

593
00:48:15,268 --> 00:48:18,021
Without Lee Mi-do in your life,
you have nothing, right?

594
00:48:19,439 --> 00:48:20,982
You're completely empty, aren't you?

595
00:48:23,067 --> 00:48:24,569
Don't live like that.

596
00:48:25,194 --> 00:48:27,113
Please don't live an empty life

597
00:48:27,238 --> 00:48:28,948
with nothing of your own,

598
00:48:30,241 --> 00:48:32,035
all for Lee Mi-do.

599
00:48:50,219 --> 00:48:51,554
Say that again.

600
00:48:52,639 --> 00:48:56,267
Say what you just said again.

601
00:48:59,812 --> 00:49:02,565
Without Lee Mi-do in your life,
you have nothing, right?

602
00:49:03,650 --> 00:49:05,068
You're completely empty, aren't you?

603
00:49:17,914 --> 00:49:18,998
Yes, you're right.

604
00:49:20,541 --> 00:49:22,251
To me, Lee Mi-do is everything.

605
00:49:23,920 --> 00:49:27,799
And since she's my everything,
I'd do anything for her.

606
00:49:30,551 --> 00:49:32,637
Even if she loves another man?

607
00:49:35,515 --> 00:49:36,974
And she leaves you for him?

608
00:49:37,100 --> 00:49:37,934
Yes.

609
00:49:38,726 --> 00:49:39,852
I'll wait for her.

610
00:49:40,812 --> 00:49:42,271
Because she'll come back to me.

611
00:49:44,691 --> 00:49:45,525
Actually,

612
00:49:47,068 --> 00:49:48,528
it's fine even if she doesn't.

613
00:49:49,946 --> 00:49:52,407
Like you said,
I'm nothing without Lee Mi-do.

614
00:49:53,032 --> 00:49:54,367
Without her,

615
00:49:54,992 --> 00:49:57,662
I wouldn't even be here to begin with, so...

616
00:49:58,538 --> 00:50:00,581
don't act like you know anything about me.

617
00:50:00,707 --> 00:50:03,751
My life is shitty enough,
so don't you dare pity me.

618
00:50:14,053 --> 00:50:15,096
Are you disappointed?

619
00:50:17,223 --> 00:50:18,141
Yes.

620
00:50:19,726 --> 00:50:21,060
I am.

621
00:50:23,229 --> 00:50:24,272
But...

622
00:50:26,691 --> 00:50:28,735
I still think you're wonderful.

623
00:50:30,194 --> 00:50:33,656
Seeing you love someone
with all your heart

624
00:50:33,781 --> 00:50:35,575
frustrates me.

625
00:50:37,285 --> 00:50:38,703
And it makes me so mad.

626
00:50:41,539 --> 00:50:43,166
Yet you're still so amazing.

627
00:50:46,294 --> 00:50:47,920
You're truly wonderful.

628
00:51:12,695 --> 00:51:15,156
50 GOOD THINGS ABOUT NAMGUNG HO

629
00:51:18,034 --> 00:51:19,494
1. HE TAKES CHARGE AND SOLVES EVERY CRISIS

630
00:51:19,619 --> 00:51:21,621
2. HE KEEPS HIS MANNERS
EVEN WITH THOSE HE DISLIKES

631
00:51:48,314 --> 00:51:49,774
Do you hate that she's remarrying?

632
00:51:49,899 --> 00:51:52,151
Keep it down. Sang-su will hear you.

633
00:51:52,985 --> 00:51:53,945
He knows.

634
00:51:56,197 --> 00:51:57,240
What?

635
00:51:58,533 --> 00:51:59,784
You know too?

636
00:52:04,497 --> 00:52:05,373
You too?

637
00:52:13,840 --> 00:52:17,093
Honestly, I thought
I was a pretty chill ex.

638
00:52:18,177 --> 00:52:20,721
But I couldn't even congratulate her.

639
00:52:22,515 --> 00:52:23,850
Oh, man.

640
00:52:23,975 --> 00:52:25,393
Then go get her back.

641
00:52:30,565 --> 00:52:32,358
You still love her, don't you?

642
00:52:33,401 --> 00:52:34,652
Go get her back.

643
00:52:35,528 --> 00:52:37,572
Come on.

644
00:52:37,697 --> 00:52:38,865
Are you crazy?

645
00:52:40,908 --> 00:52:42,118
It can't be helped.

646
00:52:42,660 --> 00:52:44,120
Don't worry about it.

647
00:52:44,912 --> 00:52:46,789
Just take good care of your wife.

648
00:52:47,915 --> 00:52:48,875
Yes, sir.

649
00:53:04,348 --> 00:53:06,392
Cut the bullshit about falling over.

650
00:53:06,517 --> 00:53:07,768
What happened?

651
00:53:09,854 --> 00:53:11,981
It's nothing. Don't worry about it.

652
00:53:23,659 --> 00:53:24,827
Is something wrong?

653
00:53:28,456 --> 00:53:29,624
Is it because of him?

654
00:53:38,466 --> 00:53:39,717
You like her, don't you?

655
00:53:45,348 --> 00:53:46,432
You like Park Su-a,

656
00:53:47,475 --> 00:53:49,018
don't you?

657
00:53:49,143 --> 00:53:51,020
Where is this coming from?

658
00:53:51,604 --> 00:53:52,897
Hey, who do you think I...

659
00:53:57,276 --> 00:53:58,319
Forget it. Drop it.

660
00:53:59,862 --> 00:54:01,948
Don't tell Yeong-do or Wan-do.

661
00:54:02,073 --> 00:54:03,282
They'll only worry.

662
00:54:05,952 --> 00:54:06,827
Stop liking her.

663
00:54:18,422 --> 00:54:21,217
Stop liking her.

664
00:54:36,232 --> 00:54:37,942
Wake me up at 9:00 a.m.

665
00:54:38,067 --> 00:54:39,318
I can't miss this.

666
00:54:42,029 --> 00:54:44,615
I don't want you to regret it like I do.

667
00:54:47,410 --> 00:54:50,663
You know what I did...

668
00:54:52,581 --> 00:54:53,916
to Bo-ra.

669
00:54:55,167 --> 00:54:56,085
Whatever.

670
00:54:57,628 --> 00:54:59,213
Stop worrying and go to sleep.

671
00:55:07,179 --> 00:55:09,473
QUEENS HAIR SALON

672
00:55:21,527 --> 00:55:24,321
<i>Park Su-a caught the kid
who stole my phone.</i>

673
00:55:24,447 --> 00:55:27,158
<i>She found the pawnshop
and is on her way there.</i>

674
00:55:27,283 --> 00:55:29,660
<i>My wife's appendix burst, so I can't go.</i>

675
00:55:29,785 --> 00:55:33,289
<i>Gangs run places like that,
so it's dangerous.</i>

676
00:55:33,414 --> 00:55:34,665
<i>Please go check on her.</i>

677
00:55:34,790 --> 00:55:36,834
<i>Su-a won't listen to me.</i>

678
00:56:19,126 --> 00:56:20,127
The pirate ship.

679
00:56:22,129 --> 00:56:24,340
Let's go ride the pirate ship.

680
00:56:57,164 --> 00:57:00,084
<i>You have left the route. Recalculating.</i>

681
00:57:13,180 --> 00:57:16,767
<i>You like Park Su-a, don't you?</i>

682
00:57:18,477 --> 00:57:19,395
<i>Mr. Namgung.</i>

683
00:57:20,855 --> 00:57:22,648
<i>I want to make you happy</i>

684
00:57:23,566 --> 00:57:25,317
every single second

685
00:57:26,026 --> 00:57:27,778
we spend together,

686
00:57:29,780 --> 00:57:32,283
not just for a second.

687
00:57:34,910 --> 00:57:37,037
That's my goal.

688
00:58:03,105 --> 00:58:04,773
Got that old lady's money?

689
00:58:04,899 --> 00:58:05,900
Oh, right. Shit.

690
00:58:10,863 --> 00:58:12,531
I got caught red-handed.

691
00:58:13,574 --> 00:58:14,950
I don't think she's a cop,

692
00:58:16,076 --> 00:58:17,077
but she's crazy.

693
00:58:18,913 --> 00:58:20,122
FRIENDLY DAILY LOANS

694
00:58:20,247 --> 00:58:21,415
I'll make this quick.

695
00:58:22,291 --> 00:58:24,710
Wednesday, April 22, 7:22.

696
00:58:24,835 --> 00:58:27,463
Outside Exit 1 of Sindaebang Station,
a man in his forties--

697
00:58:27,588 --> 00:58:30,966
actually, more like his fifties--
was waiting for a driver.

698
00:58:31,091 --> 00:58:32,384
You stole his phone, right?

699
00:58:33,177 --> 00:58:34,053
Give it back.

700
00:58:37,556 --> 00:58:38,933
This girl's got no fear.

701
00:58:39,058 --> 00:58:40,267
To catch this girl,

702
00:58:40,392 --> 00:58:42,811
I stayed up three nights
at Sindaebang Station.

703
00:58:42,937 --> 00:58:45,105
So I have no sense of fear at this point.

704
00:58:45,898 --> 00:58:48,817
Return the phone, and I'll leave quietly.

705
00:58:48,943 --> 00:58:52,112
Lady, as soon you set foot in here,

706
00:58:52,863 --> 00:58:54,907
leaving quietly stopped being an option.

707
00:59:03,749 --> 00:59:05,668
I had a good hand, too.

708
00:59:32,236 --> 00:59:33,112
POLICE

709
00:59:34,321 --> 00:59:35,155
<i>Hello?</i>

710
00:59:35,990 --> 00:59:36,991
<i>Go ahead.</i>

711
00:59:37,658 --> 00:59:39,034
<i>Are you in danger?</i>

712
00:59:57,970 --> 00:59:59,471
<i>Hello? Go ahead.</i>

713
01:00:00,389 --> 01:00:02,057
<i>Are you in danger?</i>

714
01:00:02,182 --> 01:00:03,851
Good thing I had this ready.

715
01:00:13,444 --> 01:00:15,070
Hello?

716
01:00:15,195 --> 01:00:18,490
I'd like to report a pawnshop
that sells stolen phones.

717
01:00:18,615 --> 01:00:20,159
I have evidence, too.

718
01:00:21,660 --> 01:00:23,162
The location is...

719
01:00:49,021 --> 01:00:50,189
Are you that scared?

720
01:00:54,151 --> 01:00:56,820
Are you really that scared of Namgung Ho

721
01:00:58,489 --> 01:00:59,948
liking her?

722
01:01:11,335 --> 01:01:14,129
What can I do so you won't be scared?

723
01:01:22,971 --> 01:01:24,723
How about trying to like me more?

724
01:01:27,768 --> 01:01:29,103
Try to like me...

725
01:01:31,688 --> 01:01:33,273
more than Namgung Ho.

726
01:01:40,447 --> 01:01:41,615
I'll treat you right.

727
01:01:53,710 --> 01:01:55,087
Please just like me.

728
01:03:01,278 --> 01:03:02,654
SAMHWA MOVIES

729
01:03:02,821 --> 01:03:05,157
A SCREEN SHAPED BY TIME,
STILL LIGHTING UP TODAY

730
01:03:05,282 --> 01:03:07,951
50 GOOD THINGS ABOUT NAMGUNG HO

731
01:03:09,286 --> 01:03:10,370
HUNMIN CAUGHT SWAPPING
KOREAN SWEET POTATOES FOR CHEAP IMPORTS

732
01:03:10,496 --> 01:03:11,538
<i>Who took your files?</i>

733
01:03:11,663 --> 01:03:13,582
<i>You'll get in trouble
if you keep getting involved.</i>

734
01:03:13,707 --> 01:03:15,751
<i>Why can't you give in even once?</i>

735
01:03:15,876 --> 01:03:16,877
<i>I'm the one who gives in to you.</i>

736
01:03:17,002 --> 01:03:20,797
You tore open my deepest wound,
and I'm still seeing you.

737
01:03:20,923 --> 01:03:23,425
Hilarious. Mi-do really is giving in.

738
01:03:23,550 --> 01:03:26,637
<i>I'm the one who wants to completely forget
about someone like you, got that?</i>

739
01:03:26,762 --> 01:03:28,764
<i>Then let's both try hard to forget.</i>

740
01:03:28,889 --> 01:03:31,892
<i>I take back telling you</i>

741
01:03:32,559 --> 01:03:33,644
<i>to stop liking her.</i>

742
01:03:34,853 --> 01:03:36,813
Subtitle translation by Soya Back (백소야)
